<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 March, from 222 to 1996.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elagabalus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">222 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,804 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Praetorian Guard murders Emperor Elagabalus and his mother</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Praetorian Guard killed the teenage emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus">Elagabalus</a>, whose religious innovations had caused scandal, together with his mother, Julia Soaemias. His cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severus-alexander">Severus Alexander</a>, the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severan-dynasty">Severan dynasty</a>, succeeded him.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus">Elagabalus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severus-alexander">Severus Alexander</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1261">1261 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">765 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nicaea and Genoa conclude the Treaty of Nymphaeum against Venice</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Nicaean emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a> and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> concluded a trade and defence pact at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nymphaion">Nymphaeum</a>. Genoa promised naval help against the Latin Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in return for tax-free trade and access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-nymphaeum-1261">Treaty of Nymphaeum</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1519">1519 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hernán Cortés lands on the Mexican coast</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cortés's expedition of about 500 men reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabasco">Tabasco</a> coast. Within two and a half years, with Indigenous allies, he overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1639">1639 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">387 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New College in Massachusetts is named after John Harvard</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The college at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambridge">Cambridge</a> took the name of John Harvard, a young minister who left it his library and half his estate. Founded in 1636, Harvard is the oldest university in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1781">1781 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">245 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Herschel discovers Uranus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">From his garden in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Bath</a>, Herschel spotted an object he first took for a comet. It proved to be a new planet, the first discovered with a telescope, doubling the known size of the solar system.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1881">1881 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Alexander II assassinated in St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Members of the revolutionary group People's Will threw bombs at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a>'s carriage. Alexander, who had freed the serfs, died within hours, and his son's reign brought harsh reaction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Winter War ends as the Moscow Peace Treaty takes effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> ceded about a tenth of its territory, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Its stubborn defence had cost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> heavily and preserved Finnish independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1996">1996 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">30 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunman kills 16 children and their teacher at Dunblane</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Hamilton opened fire in the gym of Dunblane Primary School in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> before killing himself. Public campaigning led to a near-total ban on private handgun ownership in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 13 March <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-duke-of-orleans"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-i-duke-of-orleans.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis I, Duke of Orléans</span><span class="tp">1372–1407</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-louis-count-of-nassau-dillenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-louis-count-of-nassau-dillenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Louis, Count of Nassau-Dillenburg</span><span class="tp">1560–1620</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georges-de-la-tour"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georges-de-la-tour.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georges de La Tour</span><span class="tp">1593–1652</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-xii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-innocent-xii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Innocent XII</span><span class="tp">1615–1700</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-seferis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-seferis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Seferis</span><span class="tp">1900–1971</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 13 March <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-iii-the-old"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mieszko-iii-the-old.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mieszko III the Old</span><span class="tp">c. 1126–1202</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johann-friedrich-bottger"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johann-friedrich-bottger.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johann Friedrich Böttger</span><span class="tp">1682–1719</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/susan-b-anthony"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Susan B. Anthony</span><span class="tp">1820–1906</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johan-laidoner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johan-laidoner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johan Laidoner</span><span class="tp">1884–1953</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fan-noli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fan Noli</span><span class="tp">1882–1965</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ivo-andric"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ivo-andric.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ivo Andrić</span><span class="tp">1892–1975</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
